  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Shivajee Ramkrishan Gupta vs State Of Maharashtra on 19 December, 2023 Author: N. J. Jamadar Bench: N. J. Jamadar 914-aba-3560-202 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No.3560 Of 2023 Shivajee Ramkrishan Gupta ...Applicant vs. The State of Maharashtra ...Respondent Mr. Ravi Gupta, for the Applicant Mr.. App, for the Respondent/State. Coram : N. J. Jamadar, J. Date : December 19, 2023 P.C.:",
    "facts": "This is an Application for pre-arrest bail in connection with C.R. No. 608 of 2023 registered at Kashimira police station for the offences punishable under sections 328, 272 and 273 r/w. 34 of Indian penal Code, 1860 and sections 26(2)(i) and 26(2)(iv) of Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006. The Applicant was protected by order dated 19/12/2023. 3. The allegations pertain to contraband article - Gutakha Pan Masala, which was seized from the co-accused and who had named the present Applicant. 4. Learned APP on instructions of the officer of the concerned police station (who is present in the Court) submits that the Applicant has co- 106.ABA.3560.2023.doc operated with the investigating and charge-sheet is ready to be filed but the same is not filed due to pendency of present Application. It is further informed that the case is already registered as SC/409/2025 with District and Sessions Court, Thane. Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/172814467/ 1 that charge-sheet in respect of the other co-accused is already filed.",
    "arguments": "4. The learned Counsel for the applicant submits that the applicability of Section 328 of IPC is debatable.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4. The learned Counsel for the applicant submits that the applicability of Section 328 of IPC is debatable.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
